SUMMARY:Life Long Learning: The History of American Anti-Semitic Terrorism & Current Threats with Stuart Wexler
DESCRIPTION:Given the current climate of anti-Semitism in our country\, Stuart Wexler will discuss the history of anti-Semitic violence\nin the United States and its relevance to today’s situation. His work explores how anti-Semitic violence and racial terrorism are often driven by the same overlooked ideologies\, a connection that is as relevant today as it was 60 years ago. \nAbout the speaker: Stuart Wexler is a historian and a teacher\, who specializes in the history of American domestic terrorism. He is the author of 4 books including America’s Secret Jihad: The Hidden History of Religious Terrorism in the United States. \nFREE for JCC Member; $15 Nonmember\n \nRegister Here\n  \nGrandchildren home on college break are welcome to attend for free.
URL:https://jccmetrowest.org/event/lll-history-of-american-anti-semitic-terrorism/
LOCATION:JCC MetroWest | Tepper Hall\, 760 Northfield Ave\, West Orange\, NJ\, 07052\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Enrichment
