SUMMARY:Book Group: Emily Franklin
DESCRIPTION:Love & Other Monsters by Emily Franklin\nInspired by the extraordinary summer of 1816 that gave birth to Frankenstein\, Love & Other Monsters reimagines the life of Claire Clairmont—the overlooked stepsister of Mary Shelley—as she navigates love\, ambition\, betrayal\, and the creative passions of history’s most legendary literary circle. Rich in atmosphere and emotional depth\, this evocative novel explores the women whose stories have too often been left out of literary history. \nBook group discussion at 12:00 PM\nAuthor presentation at 1:00 PM \nBook Group discussion and conversation with the author will be available either in person or on Zoom for participants; author will present via Zoom. \nFREE for Members; $15 Nonmember \nRegister Here\n\nIn partnership with: \n         
URL:https://jccmetrowest.org/event/book-group-emily-franklin/
LOCATION:JCC MetroWest | Goldstein Room\, 760 Northfield Ave\, West Orange\, NJ\, 07052\, United States
CATEGORIES:Center for the Arts,The Gaelen
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jccmetrowest.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/BookGroup26-27_Emily-Franklin_HERO.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Katy Strulson":MAILTO:kstrulson@jccmetrowest.org
END:VEVENT
